module

public import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.GroupScheme.ReductiveBorelPairStructure
public import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.GroupScheme.RationalHighestWeightData
import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.GroupScheme.BorelRootProductCoordinates

/-! # Infinitesimal simplicity of restricted highest-weight modules

Source: Milne, Algebraic Groups (2017), Section 22(e), statement 22.54, p.481.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-restricted-module-infinitesimal-simplicity)

Restriction is measured by simple-coroot pairings, equivalently coefficients of
fundamental weights. The source's displayed simple-root coefficients are a typo,
already corrected in the DAG statement. The Lie algebra is written directly as
linear maps on the coordinate ring satisfying the Leibniz identity at the counit;
its action is contraction of the given coaction, followed by the tensor right unitor.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u v

open CategoryTheory MonoidalCategory CartesianMonoidalCategory
open scoped MonObj TensorProduct

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.RationalHighestWeight

/-- A simple rational module with restricted highest weight for a semisimple simply
connected group has no proper nonzero subspace stable under its differential action.
Source: Milne, Section 22(e), statement 22.54, p.481; restricted means simple-coroot
pairings in [0,p), as specified in the DAG, rather than simple-root coefficients.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-restricted-module-infinitesimal-simplicity)

Proof plan:
1. Choose a nonzero U-invariant highest vector v. The Borel-pair structure gives
   B = U semidirect T, so v is a B-eigenvector. Simplicity makes it cyclic.
   lem-sfb-primitive-cyclic-weight-bound gives that its weight space is the line Fv.
2. Let A be the unital algebra generated by the differential operators and D = Av.
   Conjugating dual-number points gives the adjoint conjugation identity for the
   differential, after every scalar extension. Tangent spaces commute with these
   extensions because they are duals of the finite-dimensional augmentation
   cotangent space. Thus A is scheme-theoretically normalized. Apply
   lem-sfb-normalized-algebra-weight-line-simple to see that D is a simple A-module.
3. For each simple root use lem-sfb-opposite-root-sl2-parametrizations and
   lem-sfb-borel-root-product-coordinates. The upper root subgroup fixes v and the
   diagonal has weight m = pairing(lambda,coroot), with 0 <= m < p. By
   lem-sfb-sl2-highest-orbit-polynomial, the lower orbit of v is the sum of
   a^j times f^j(v)/j! for 0 <= j <= m. Every term belongs to D after base change.
4. The torus preserves Fv. Normalization of A and step 3 show that the torus and
   both simple root subgroups preserve D in both directions. The equations that
   the lower-left blocks of rho(g) and rho(g inverse) vanish define the closed
   subgroup stabilizing D. By lem-sfb-simple-root-generation-mixed-commutation it
   is the whole group. At the universal coordinate-valued point this says that D
   is a rational submodule of V.
5. Simplicity and v nonzero give D = V. A subspace stable under all differential
   operators is stable under their generated unital algebra A. Simplicity from
   step 2 therefore makes it zero or V. Only factorials j! with j < p were inverted,
   so p = 2 is included. With empty simple-root base the generation assertion says
   G = T; weight zero gives constant root-orbit polynomials. Products need no change.
-/
theorem restricted_module_infinitesimal_simplicity
    {F : Type u} [Field F] [IsAlgClosed F] (p : ℕ) [CharP F p] (hp : 0 < p)
    (G T B U : Grp (Over (Spec (.of F))))
    [IsAffine G.X.left] [IsAffine T.X.left] [IsAffine U.X.left]
    (hG : IsSemisimpleGroupScheme G.X)
    (hsc : ∀ (G' : Over (Spec (.of F))) [GrpObj G'],
      IsSemisimpleGroupScheme G' → ∀ (f : G' ⟶ G.X) [IsMonHom f],
      Surjective f.left → IsFinite (GrpObj.ker f).hom →
      (∀ (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [Algebra F A]
        (x : StandardGroupSchemes.affine F A ⟶ GrpObj.ker f)
        (g : StandardGroupSchemes.affine F A ⟶ G'),
        (x ≫ GrpObj.kerι f) * g = g * (x ≫ GrpObj.kerι f)) → IsIso f)
    (iT : T ⟶ G) (iB : B ⟶ G) (j : T ⟶ B) (iU : U ⟶ B)
    (hT : ReductiveTorusCentralizer.IsMaximalTorus iT)
    (hsplit : ∃ r : ℕ, Nonempty (T ≅ MultiplicativeType.splitTorus F r))
    (hB : IsBorelGroupScheme iB.hom.hom) (hj : j ≫ iB = iT)
    (hUclosed : IsClosedSubgroupScheme iU.hom.hom)
    (hUnormal : IsNormalSubgroupScheme iU.hom.hom)
    (hUsmooth : Smooth U.X.hom) (hUconnected : ConnectedSpace U.X.left)
    (hUunipotent : SolvableGroupStructure.IsUnipotent U)
    (hUmax : ∀ (N : Grp (Over (Spec (.of F)))) (iN : N ⟶ B),
      IsClosedSubgroupScheme iN.hom.hom → IsNormalSubgroupScheme iN.hom.hom →
      Smooth N.X.hom → ConnectedSpace N.X.left →
      SolvableGroupStructure.IsUnipotent N → ∃ f : N ⟶ U, f ≫ iU = iN)
    [IsCommMonObj T.X] [IsCommMonObj (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F)]
    (aG : ModObj T.X G.X) (aB : ModObj T.X B.X)
    (haG : aG.smul = (iT.hom.hom ⊗ₘ 𝟙 G.X) ≫ GrpObj.conj G.X)
    (haB : aB.smul = (j.hom.hom ⊗ₘ 𝟙 B.X) ≫ GrpObj.conj B.X)
    (Φ : Finset (Additive (T ⟶ Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F))))
    (P : RootDatum Φ
      (Additive (T ⟶ Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F)))
      (Additive (Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F) ⟶ T)))
    (b : P.Base)
    (hroot : ∀ α : Φ, P.root α = α.val)
    (hpair : ∀ (χ : Additive (T ⟶ Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F)))
      (ν : Additive (Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F) ⟶ T)),
      ν.toMul.hom.hom ≫ χ.toMul.hom.hom =
        (𝟙 (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F)) ^ (P.toLinearMap χ ν))
    (hweights : ∀ χ : Additive (T ⟶ Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F)),
      χ ∈ Φ ↔ χ ≠ 0 ∧ @TorusCharacterTangent.weightSpace F _ T G aG χ.toMul ≠ ⊥)
    (hpositive : ∀ α : Φ,
      b.IsPos α ↔ @TorusCharacterTangent.weightSpace F _ T B aB α.val.toMul ≠ ⊥)
    {V : Type v} [AddCommGroup V] [Module F V] [FiniteDimensional F V]
    (c : V →ₗ[F] V ⊗[F] coordinateAlgebra G)
    (hcoassoc : HopfAction.Coassociative F (coordinateAlgebra G) V c)
    (hcounit : HopfAction.Counital F (coordinateAlgebra G) V c)
    (hsimple : IsSimple c)
    (lam : T ⟶ Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F))
    (hhighest : HasHighestWeight c iT (iU ≫ iB) lam)
    (hrestricted : ∀ α : b.support,
      0 ≤ P.toLinearMap (Additive.ofMul lam) (P.coroot α) ∧
      P.toLinearMap (Additive.ofMul lam) (P.coroot α) < (p : ℤ)) :
    ∀ N : Submodule F V,
      (∀ x : coordinateAlgebra G →ₗ[F] F,
        (∀ a d : coordinateAlgebra G,
          x (a * d) = Coalgebra.counit (R := F) a * x d +
            x a * Coalgebra.counit (R := F) d) →
        ∀ v ∈ N, (TensorProduct.rid F V) (x.lTensor V (c v)) ∈ N) →
      N = ⊥ ∨ N = ⊤ := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.RationalHighestWeight
